      </figure>
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;font-size:24px;margin-bottom:12px">Pain → less movement → less warmth → stiffer joint → more pain.</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);margin-bottom:12px">It's why your knees are worst in the morning, worse in winter, and seize up after sitting. The joint cools down, blood flow drops, and everything tightens.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);margin-bottom:12px">A ten-minute heat pack interrupts the loop. Then it goes cold, and the loop closes again. To actually loosen a stiff knee, the warmth has to be <strong style="color:var(--ink)">deep, even, and repeated daily</strong> — which is exactly what nothing in your cupboard can do.</p>
